      "text": "On canonical triangulations of once-punctured torus bundles and two-bridge link complements Introduction — 29 sections: Front matter; Introduction; Conjugacy in SL(2,Z) and the Farey\n\n**On canonical triangulations of once-punctured torus bundles and two-bridge link complements Introduction**\n\n*FRANC¸OIS GUÉRITAUD*\n\n46 pp, 29 sections.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Conjugacy in SL(2,Z) and the Farey tesselati; 3 The canonical triangulation; 3.1 Diagonal exchanges; 3.2 Tetrahedra; 4 Combinatorics of the torus at infinity; 5 Finding positive angles; 6 Hyperbolic volume; 6.1 Volume of an ideal tetrahedron; 6.2 Critical volume and trivial holonomy; 6.3 Behavior of the volume functional; 7 Ruling out some degeneracies; 8 A geometrical lemma; 9 Ruling out all degeneracies; 9.1 Case 1: RR|LR; 9.2 Case 2: RR|LL; 10 A numerical example",
